is is conflicting. \n\nIn this case, the user needs to check the logs for the user-service pod to see if there are any errors. But without the exact pod name, they can\'t do that. So the next step is to get the pod name first. \n\nTherefore, the correct tool call is to run `kubectl get pods -n social-network` again to get the exact pod name for user-service. Once they have that, they can then retrieve the logs.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get pods -n social-network"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1222, 'prompt_tokens': 2614, 'total_tokens': 3836, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbeb-49d7-7780-8696-4663147fa9c5-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2614, 'output_tokens': 1222, 'total_tokens': 3836}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b50584fb-02ea-4c50-aa9f-ac88d705c5aa'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose a social network application composed of many microservices. They\'ve already checked the deployments and pods, and everything seems to be running with the READY status as 1/1. But the user is concerned about potential faults in some services.\n\nEarlier, they tried to get the logs for the user-service pod, but the command was rejected because they didn\'t specify the exact pod name. The error message mentioned a ValueError about write redirection being forbidden, which probably means they tried to use an interactive command or a flag that\'s not allowed. Since the tool only allows read-only comm